    tagline: "A child genius trained to command humanity's fleet — and the moral weight of what he does with that training",
    description: "Orson Scott Card's Ender's Game drops Andrew Wiggin into Battle School at age six: a zero-gravity military training facility where children are evaluated for the role of humanity's supreme commander against the Formics, an alien species that has attacked Earth twice. The novel is about strategy and genius and psychological manipulation — and about what the people who need Ender to be what they've made him are actually doing to him. The ending, which reframes everything that came before, has been discussed in philosophy and ethics courses for 40 years. If the tactical puzzle-solving, the isolation-as-training theme, the moral weight of child soldiers, and the twist gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
