    description: "Naomi Novik's A Deadly Education is the first book in the Scholomance trilogy. The Scholomance is a school for magical students that is designed to produce graduates by killing everyone else — no teachers, no staff, no protection except what students can build for themselves from their courses. El (Galadriel) has a prophesied ability to cause mass death, which everyone around her assumes means she will become a dark mage. She is very tired of being assumed about. The novel is narrated by El in a voice that is one of the most distinctive in recent YA fantasy — caustic, precise, and often very funny about things that are terrible. If the mordant heroine, the death-trap school, the slow-burn romance with an annoyingly competent savior, and the world-building that works out what magical student debt actually is gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
