    description: "Tim O'Brien's The Things They Carried (1990) is the most important American war writing of its generation — Alpha Company in Vietnam, the question of what fiction can do that facts cannot, and the cargo that soldiers carry home. If you were drawn to its formal invention and its moral seriousness, these novels and memoirs will find you in the same place.",
