    tagline: 'What to read after Steppenwolf by Hermann Hesse',
    description: "Hermann Hesse's Steppenwolf (1927) is the great novel of the divided self — Harry Haller, half-man and half-wolf, unable to fit into bourgeois society, who enters the Magic Theatre and discovers that there is not one self but many. If you were drawn to its exploration of inner division and its refusal of the comfortable middle, these novels will find you in the same territory.",
