    tagline: 'What to read after Their Eyes Were Watching God by Zora Neale Hurston',
    description: "Zora Neale Hurston's Their Eyes Were Watching God (1937) is a landmark of American literature — Janie Crawford's story of three marriages and her search for love and selfhood in early twentieth-century Florida, told in a prose that draws on the full richness of the Black American vernacular tradition. Neglected for decades and now recognized as one of the great American novels. These books will find you in the same territory.",
    keywords: ['books like Their Eyes Were Watching God', 'books like Their Eyes Were Watching God Zora Neale Hurston', 'hurston similar books', 'black literature similar books', 'what to read after Their Eyes Were Watching God', 'zora neale hurston recommendations'],
