    description: "Graham Greene's The Quiet American (1955) is a masterwork of political fiction — Fowler's weary moral pragmatism against Pyle's dangerous innocent certainty, with 1950s Saigon as the backdrop. Still the most prescient literary critique of American interventionism in Southeast Asia, and a perfect miniature of what Greene does at his best. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
