    description: "John Galsworthy's The Forsyte Saga (beginning with A Man of Property, 1906) is the great English family saga of the Victorian and Edwardian middle class — Soames Forsyte, who owns everything and cannot possess the one thing he wants. The Nobel Prize-winning portrait of an England in the process of becoming something else. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
