    description: "Theodor Fontane's Effi Briest (1895) is the masterwork of German literary realism — a seventeen-year-old girl married to a much older Prussian official, destroyed by the social consequences of a brief affair that ended years before her destruction. Thomas Mann called it one of the six greatest novels ever written. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
