    tagline: 'What to read after Under Western Eyes by Joseph Conrad',
    description: "Joseph Conrad's Under Western Eyes (1911) is the most politically complex of his major novels — Razumov's inadvertent betrayal in St. Petersburg, his forced career as a double agent in Geneva, and the weight of guilt that the narrator describes from the outside. Conrad's explicit response to Dostoevsky and the Russian political novel. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
