    tagline: "What to read after The Stranger by Albert Camus",
    description: "Albert Camus's The Stranger (L'Étranger, 1942) is the defining work of philosophical absurdism — Meursault's radical emotional honesty, his killing of an Arab, his trial, and his death-cell recognition. The novel that made existentialism accessible to a generation and that still starts more philosophical arguments than almost any other. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
