    description: "Thomas Mann's Doctor Faustus (1947) is his most personal and most ambitious novel — Adrian Leverkühn's pact with the Devil, the destruction of German culture, and the question of whether artistic genius and moral catastrophe are necessarily linked. The most complete literary reckoning with National Socialism by a major German writer. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
