    description: "In Our Time is Hemingway's breakthrough — the collection that established his prose method and the iceberg theory that would define American short fiction for the next generation. If the compression, the implication, and the emotional territory of the Nick Adams stories moved you, these books share his formal innovation, his portrait of the aftermath of World War I, and his ability to say the important things by not saying them.",
