    description: "Moby-Dick is the great American novel — a meditation on obsession, fate, and the sublime indifference of nature. If you've conquered Melville's white whale, these books share its philosophical ambition, its willingness to embed ideas deep within narrative, and its interest in humanity's struggle against forces larger than itself.",
