    description: "Hamlet is the tragedy of overthinking — a prince who sees too clearly to act, and whose clarity destroys everything. If Shakespeare's play haunts you with its questions about thought, action, and mortality, these books share its meditation on indecision, grief, the performance of identity, and what it costs to know too much.",
